Subject: [PATCH] engine: every unsatisfiable tensor split exits 86, not just one

Only one of the ways a tensor split can fail to describe a tensor was graceful.
The other 38 still aborted, so a model hitting any of them died with a bare assert
after the weights had loaded and the app had no chance to recover.

All of them now go through one helper that reports the reason and exits 86, which
is what Server.swift watches for, so the app retries once with --split-mode layer.
TOSH_TENSOR_SPLIT_STRICT=1 keeps every one of them as an abort.

Converted: unsupported mul_mat split states, shape mismatch, unimplemented op,
inconsistent split ratio, unresolved split axis, unresolvable source axis, permuted
view, segmented reshape/permute/transpose, matmul operands split differently,
batched matmul operands split differently, split width not a block multiple,
split widths not summing to the tensor, multi-segment state, add with a non-mirrored
id source, concat along the split axis, per-row op on a column-split tensor,
set_rows, rope with a split position tensor, pad with a non-zero offset,
flash attention mirrors, lightning indexer mirrors, ssm_conv sources and state.

set_rows was not hypothetical: GGML_METAL_WAVE64_DECODE_DISABLE=1 changed the graph
shape enough to reach the set_rows assert and kill llama-bench.

